    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "TWA\nOVERNICHI\nCOAST tO COAST\nDOUGLAS\nAIRLINERS\nON ALL\nSCHEDULES\nT\n• THE • LINDBERGH• LINE•",
      "FULL HEAD ROOM\nUNOBSIKUCIED AISLE\nCOLD AIR VENTI\nLATING DUCI\nSTEAM HEATING\nDIKECIIONAL BEAM\nGERS.\nSALON IS COMPLETELY SOUND\nPROOFED AGAINST ALL NOISE\nQUISTER THAN A PIIMAN\nAND\nDOUGLAS\nAIR RRAKEC\n• RADICA\nSPEED TO\nRADIO ANTENNA\n• WAY VOICE RADIO MAIN.\nTAINS CONTACT BETWEEN\nGROUND AND PLANE.\nALSO\nFOR WEATHER AND DIRAC\nHIONAL BEAM SIGNALS.\nGIVE A SPEED OF 210M. P. H\nAT 8000 FT.\nSPACIOUS PILOT'S COM\nPARTMENT WITH COM\nPLETE DAY AND NIGHI\nCARGO COMMAND.\nICED BUFFET AND SERVICE CABINET.\nCOMPLE ESKEAMLINING. NOIE\nMEIHOD\n\"FLOWING\" ONE SUR\nFACE INTO ANOTHER.\nTING TO HIGH SPEED PERFORMANCE.\nVENTILATION INTAKE.\nLANDING LIGHTS.\nDOOR TO 76 CU. FT. MAIL\nCOMPARTMENT.\nHEELS RETRACT INI\nINDIVIDUAL READING LIGHT\nASH TRAY. SERVICE BUTTON\nAPPAKEL KACK ANDYEN ILA-\nIN CON\nTHE INTERNATIONALLY FAMOUS\nTW A Douglas Luxury Airliner\nis revolutionizing the art of flying. Discriminating air travelers everywhere are demand-\ning TWA speed and security.\nCommuting between California and New York which would have sounded fantastic\nuntil recently, is now not only a possibility but an everyday occurrence, made possible\nby TWA's overnight coast to coast service.\nWide-awake business and professional men whose time is valuable, women who enjoy\nthe luxury and simplicity of air travel, and vacationists who demand the most of their\nholiday period, are taking advantage of this popular mode of travel in greatly increasing\nYou, too, will enjoy traveling on TWA, \"The Lindbergh Line.\"\nA FEW OUTSTANDING REASONS\nfor TWA SUPREMACY\nTWA Douglas Luxury Airliners, operating on\nregular overnight service between the Atlantic\nand Pacific coasts, provide the fastest trans-\ncontinental service.\nTWA is the only airline in the world equipped\nwith syro pilot and automatic stabilizers. Only\non TWA can you enjoy the luxury, speed and\ndependability of a mighty fleet of Douglas Air-\nliners all the way from coast to coast.\nThe TWA route was personally selected by\nColonel Lindbergh as being best adapted for\nregular transcontinental service, and the excep-\ntional performance record has amply vindicated\nhis judgment.\nOnly Douglas Airliners have the comforts of\nsteam heated cabins, maintaining by thermostatic\ncontrol a constant cabin temperature of 70\ndegrees.\nThe unusually quiet cabins of the TWA Luxury\nAirliners permit conversation to be carried on\nin an ordinary tone of voice.\nVibration and\nengine noise have been practically eliminated.\nTwo 700 horsepower Wright Cyclone engines\nprovide more than sufficient reserve power to\nenable the plane to not only fly, but to take-off\nfully loaded on only one engine.\nTWA's SKY CHIEF, the criterion for all air\ntravel, is truly a limited service, making only four\nstops between California and New York.\nTWIN CITIES\nOST LOUIS\nKANSAS CITY\nLOS ANGELES\nSAN FRANCISCO\nOSAN DIEGO\nTWA has been referred to as \"The Line of the\nPresidents.\"\nThe passenger list on the SKY\nCHIEF resembles a page from Who's Who,\nnumbering business and social\nleaders from all walks of life.\nPITTSBURGH\nCOLUMBUS\nINDIANAPOLIS\nNEW YORK\nPHILADELPHIA\nI WASHINGTON\nSHORTEST ROUTE COAST TO COAST"
    ],
